# Google Places key for the nearby-places list in the location picker.
#
# Optional: without it the picker still works, it simply shows no nearby list.
#
# This is NOT the Firebase or Maps key. Places is a web service, and Google
# does not support Android app restrictions on web service keys — so this one
# cannot be locked to the app, and must never be committed. Copy this file to
# .env and put the real key there, or set it as an EAS secret:
#
#   eas secret:create --name EXPO_PUBLIC_PLACES_API_KEY --value <key>
#
# Note that EXPO_PUBLIC_ variables are embedded in the app bundle and can be
# extracted from the APK. For a key that must stay private, proxy the call
# through a Cloud Function instead — see functions/README.md.
EXPO_PUBLIC_PLACES_API_KEY=
